A) Design deltas — roles, portals, routing rules, entities
Roles / user types

Public (unauthenticated/anonymous or basic account): read-only portal: browse issues, upvote, view solutions, filters/sorting; no internal queues or triage actions.

Internal (authenticated):

Analyst: sees all internal dashboards, can tag, edit Eisenhower fields, queue for ThinkTank, propose solutions.

Lieutenant: intake for “Urgent & Not Important” (delegate/assign).

ThinkTankLead: runs sessions for “Important & Not Urgent”.

HeadOfState: final owner for “Urgent & Important”; can mark “priority of week”.

(You can collapse to a single “Internal” role with capability flags if you prefer.)

Eisenhower classification on every Issue

Add either a compact enum or a double-boolean. Recommend both for ergonomics:

isUrgent (bool)

isImportant (bool)

eisenhowerQuadrant (enum: DO_FIRST | SCHEDULE | DELEGATE | ELIMINATE)
Mapping:

DO_FIRST = Urgent & Important (U&I)

DELEGATE = Urgent & Not Important (U&¬I)

SCHEDULE = Important & Not Urgent (¬U&I)

ELIMINATE = Not Urgent & Not Important (¬U&¬I)

Daily routing (automated triage)

At 00:05 local time (configurable), run a triage job:

ELIMINATE (¬U & ¬I) ➜ move to Backlog queue (publicly visible, upvotable).

DELEGATE (U & ¬I) ➜ enqueue to Lieutenant Queue; auto-notify lieutenants; require assignment to an owner within 24h.

SCHEDULE (¬U & I) ➜ enqueue to ThinkTank Queue; visible in prep list for weekly sessions.

DO_FIRST (U & I) ➜ enqueue to HeadOfState Queue immediately; mark as High-Alert.

Weekly prioritization (internal)

Every Monday 09:00 generate a Weekly Priority Report:

Rank by composite score: priorityScore = (urgency * 0.6) + (normalized uniqueSupportersInTree * 0.25) + (similarityCount * 0.1) + (resolvesCount * 0.05).

Produce per-queue top N (configurable), with diffs vs last week.

High-Alert definition (used to surface in internal portal)

Flag High-Alert if any:

urgency >= 80, or

week-over-week upvote spike ≥ 50%, or

Eisenhower = DO_FIRST.

